at the Electric Cinema","address":"191 Portobello Road, W11","position":[51.5158,-0.2048],"positionChecked":false,"about":"One of London's oldest cinemas, with sofas and footstools. The perfect end to the day.","tips":["Book ahead for the front sofas, especially at weekends."],"flags":[],"photoSpot":false,"alertRadiusM":30,"dwellMin":150,"verified":false,"optional":false,"alternatives":[{"name":"Electric Diner","address":"191 Portobello Road, W11","why":"Dinner next door to the cinema before the film","minutesAway":0,"verified":false}],"sources":[]}],"route":{"walkKm":4,"legs":[]},"tips":["Saturday is market day: busier, but the day comes alive.","Several stops are private homes. Be brief and quiet outside them."],"extras":[{"title":"Kenwood House, Hampstead Heath","text":"Where Anna shoots her period film. Free entry, with a café. Best as a separate morning or afternoon."},{"title":"Afternoon tea at the Ritz","text":"Anna's hotel. Lovely, but expensive, and well away from Notting Hill."}],"stays":[],"related":[],"sources":[{"name":"movie-locations.com: Notting Hill","url":"https://www.movie-locations.com/movies/n/Notting-Hill.php"}]},{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"london-ted-lasso","status":"draft","lastChecked":"2026-11-17","title":"Ted Lasso","tagline":"Believe in Richmond: Ted's pub, his street and the river","kind":"series","films":[{"title":"Ted Lasso","year":2020,"imdb":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt10986410/","trailer":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3u7EIiohs6U","director":"Created by Jason Sudeikis, Bill Lawrence, Brendan Hunt and Joe Kelly","cast":["Jason Sudeikis","Hannah Waddingham","Brett Goldstein","Juno Temple","Brendan Hunt","Nick Mohammed","Phil Dunster","Jeremy Swift"]}],"aboutFilm":{"short":"An American college football coach is hired to manage AFC Richmond, a struggling English football club, even though he knows nothing about the game. His relentless kindness slowly wins over the players, the owner and the town.","more":"Jason Sudeikis plays Ted, with Hannah Waddingham as the club's owner Rebecca and Brett Goldstein as the gruff captain Roy Kent. The Apple TV+ series ran for three seasons from 2020 to 2023 and won the Emmy for best comedy series twice."},"genres":["comedy","sport"],"city":"london","area":"Richmond and Twickenham","goodFor":["mainstream","couples"],"length":"full-day","bestTime":"Any day of the week. Mornings are quieter on Richmond Green, and a dry day makes the riverside walk to Twickenham a highlight.","intro":"The show's Richmond is real: Ted's local pub, the lane where he lives and the Green where he meets the town are all a few minutes from Richmond station. In the afternoon, follow the Thames to Twickenham for Church Street and the riverside bench from Season 2, then head back to Richmond for dinner by the river.","food":{"availability":"some","note":"Richmond and Twickenham have plenty of pubs and cafés, but the riverside path between them has almost nothing for about 45 minutes. Bring water, and a snack if you're walking it with children."},"gettingThere":{"transit":[{"name":"Richmond","mode":"tube","lines":["District","Overground","trains from Waterloo"],"position":[51.463,-0.3013],"walkMin":5,"verified":false}],"parking":{"note":"Richmond town centre parking is pay-and-display and fills up at weekends. The nearest larger car park is listed below.","places":[{"name":"Old Deer Park car park","address":"Twickenham Road, Richmond","walkMin":10}],"warnings":["London's ULEZ charge applies to older cars across all of London. Check your car on the TfL website before you drive.","Richmond is outside the central Congestion Charge zone."],"verified":false},"note":"Richmond station is the start and the end of the day. From Twickenham you can take a train back, one or two stops."},"stops":[{"id":"richmond-green","time":"10:00","kind":"scene","name":"Richmond Green","address":"Richmond Green, TW9","position":[51.4613,-0.306],"positionChecked":false,"scene":"Ted crosses the Green on his way to work, and a young girl dribbles a ball past him.","tips":[],"flags":[],"photoSpot":true,"alertRadiusM":30,"dwellMin":20,"verified":true,"optional":false,"alternatives":[],"sources":[{"name":"Groundhopper Guides: Ted Lasso locations","url":"https://groundhopperguides.com/ted-lasso-filming-locations/"}]},{"id":"princes-head","time":"10:30","kind":"scene","name":"The Prince's Head (the Crown and Anchor)","address":"The Green, Richmond, TW9","position":[51.4608,-0.3051],"positionChecked":false,"scene":"The Crown and Anchor, Ted's local, where Mae pours the pints and the fans gather on match days.","tips":["The pub's outside is the one in the show, but the bar inside was rebuilt in a studio."],"flags":["myth"],"photoSpot":true,"alertRadiusM":30,"dwellMin":15,"verified":true,"optional":false,"alternatives":[],"sources":[{"name":"Groundhopper Guides: Ted Lasso locations","url":"https://groundhopperguides.com/ted-lasso-filming-locations/"}]},{"id":"paved-court","time":"10:45","kind":"scene","name":"Paved Court: Ted's street","address":"Paved Court, Richmond, TW9","position":[51.4606,-0.3048],"positionChecked":false,"scene":"The narrow lane where Ted lives, which he walks down on his way to the Green.","tips":[],"flags":[],"photoSpot":true,"alertRadiusM":30,"dwellMin":10,"verified":true,"optional":false,"alternatives":[],"sources":[{"name":"Groundhopper Guides: Ted Lasso locations","url":"https://groundhopperguides.com/ted-lasso-filming-locations/"}]},{"id":"richmond-coffee","time":"11:00","kind":"coffee","name":"Coffee in the lanes","address":"The lanes between Richmond Green and George Street","position":[51.4604,-0.3045],"positionChecked":false,"about":"The lanes around Paved Court are full of independent cafés. Pick one and take your coffee down to the river.","tips":[],"flags":[],"photoSpot":false,"alertRadiusM":30,"dwellMin":20,"verified":false,"optional":false,"alternatives":[],"sources":[]},{"id":"richmond-bridge","time":"11:30","kind":"photo","name":"Richmond riverside and bridge","address":"Richmond Riverside, TW9","position":[51.4572,-0.3068],"positionChecked":false,"about":"Not a scene from the show, but the classic view of Richmond: the 18th-century bridge and the terraces down to the Thames.","tips":[],"flags":[],"photoSpot":true,"alertRadiusM":30,"dwellMin":30,"verified":true,"optional":true,"alternatives":[],"sources":[]},{"id":"lunch-princes-head","time":"12:30","kind":"food","name":"Lunch at the Prince's Head","address":"The Green, Richmond, TW9","position":[51.4608,-0.3051],"positionChecked":false,"about":"A proper pub lunch in Ted's local. Sit outside facing the Green if the weather allows.","tips":[],"flags":[],"photoSpot":false,"alertRadiusM":30,"dwellMin":75,"verified":false,"optional":false,"alternatives":[{"name":"Chango","address":"Paved Court, Richmond","why":"Argentine empanadas to take away. The shop itself appears on Ted's street","minutesAway":1,"verified":false}],"sources":[]},{"id":"twickenham-church-street","time":"14:30","kind":"scene","name":"Church Street, Twickenham","address":"Church Street, Twickenham, TW1","position":[51.4467,-0.3292],"positionChecked":false,"scene":"Season 2 scenes on this old village street, including the shopfront used for \"Mojo\", the doll shop.","tips":["Church Street is closed to traffic at weekends, with café tables out in the road."],"flags":[],"photoSpot":false,"alertRadiusM":30,"dwellMin":30,"verified":true,"optional":false,"alternatives":[],"sources":[{"name":"Groundhopper Guides: Ted Lasso locations","url":"https://groundhopperguides.com/ted-lasso-filming-locations/"}]},{"id":"twickenham-riverside","time":"15:15","kind":"scene","name":"Twickenham riverside, opposite Eel Pie Island","address":"The Embankment, Twickenham, TW1","position":[51.4458,-0.3277],"positionChecked":false,"scene":"The boathouse and the riverside bench where Roy, Keeley and Phoebe sit and talk.","tips":["The Barmy Arms pub is right here if you want a drink by the water before heading back."],"flags":[],"photoSpot":true,"alertRadiusM":30,"dwellMin":30,"verified":true,"optional":false,"alternatives":[],"sources":[{"name":"Groundhopper Guides: Ted Lasso locations","url":"https://groundhopperguides.com/ted-lasso-filming-locations/"}]},{"id":"gaucho-richmond","time":"19:00","kind":"food","name":"Dinner at Gaucho Richmond","address":"The Towpath, Richmond Riverside, TW10","position":[51.4585,-0.3066],"positionChecked":false,"scene":"Thought to be the restaurant from the double-date scene. Not yet confirmed.","about":"Argentine steak on the river, a treat to end the day.","tips":[],"flags":[],"photoSpot":false,"alertRadiusM":30,"dwellMin":120,"verified":false,"optional":false,"alternatives":[{"name":"The Prince's Head","address":"The Green, Richmond","why":"Back to Ted's local for a cheaper, more relaxed dinner","minutesAway":8,"verified":false}],"sources":[]}],"route":{"walkKm":7,"legs":[{"from":"lunch-princes-head","to":"twickenham-church-street","mode":"walk","minutes":50,"note":"Along the Thames towpath past Marble Hill House. Or take a bus or the train (Richmond to Twickenham) if it's raining."},{"from":"twickenham-riverside","to":"gaucho-richmond","mode":"train","minutes":15,"note":"Train from Twickenham back to Richmond, then a short walk down to the river."}]},"tips":["Ted Lasso is filmed all over south-west London. This day keeps to the places you can walk between.","The Prince's Head gets busy when the show has a new season out. Go early for an outside table."],"extras":[{"title":"A match at Selhurst Park","text":"Crystal Palace's ground in South Norwood stood in for AFC Richmond's \"Nelson Road\" stadium. Going to a Palace home game is as close as you'll get to a Richmond match day."},{"title":"Hampton Court Palace","text":"A short trip from Twickenham, with its own film and TV location tour. Good for a second day in the area."}],"stays":[],"related":[],"sources":[{"name":"Groundhopper Guides: Ted Lasso locations","url":"https://groundhopperguides.com/ted-